{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Reclassified bug -> task: the concrete defect already landed with 103729e90c; what remains is process/guardrail work\n\nThe concrete convergence defect this ticket documents — a re-derived oracle blind to send-path drift — was fixed in commit `103729e90c` (\"Fit the comment dedup key like the send path\", verified reachable from origin/main): the test now captures the `--body` argument from a real `acli_cli_ops.add_comment` call with only `acli_subprocess._run_acli` stubbed, so the send side of the assertion moves with the send path.\n\nWhat remains in this ticket's acceptance criteria is process/guardrail work — decide and record the rule that convergence tests must capture the external-effect side from the real call site rather than recompute it, and make that rule discoverable/enforceable. That is designed guardrail work with no currently-broken behaviour behind it, i.e. task-shaped, not a defect. Type changed bug -> task; the evidence and ACs are unchanged."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787333929205398001,"uuid":"5248a38f-311d-4fc9-bc6b-662e73bcd0f1"}